  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Dockside City Race 10K - crowd notes\nSunday 8 August 2027 / contact Rhys Morgan 555-0152\ntotal 800 incl 800 runners. We do not expect spectators in any number beyond the runners' own companions.\n\nVIEWING\n3 barriered areas: finish the pavilion, turn at Reservoir Walk, start the old mill car park. approx 1050 total @ 2 per sqm. over expected numbers\n\nSTART\n5 waves, 4 min gaps, seeded by expected time. pens close 5 min before each wave\n\nSTEWARDS\n16 stewards (approx 1:50), 2 supervisors, rota by position, briefing 1hr before\n\nEXIT\nrunners one-way funnel to recovery, out north gate. spectators 2 marked exits, steward on each. clear in 25 mins\n\nCONTROL\nRhys Morgan at control w/ radio to all supervisors. can hold wave, stop race, use PA. sups call in if area getting full\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERTIFICATE OF LIABILITY INSURANCE\nCertificate no. AG-73171\nIssued: April 24, 2027\n\nINSURER: Northern Shield Assurance\nPOLICY NUMBER: PL-617630\n\nNAMED INSURED: Dockside Sports Trust\nDESCRIPTION OF OPERATIONS: Public liability for a foot race, the Dockside City Race 10K\nVENUE: Eastfield, Port Halden\n\nPOLICY PERIOD\nEffective: August 7, 2027\nExpiry: August 9, 2027\n\nLIMIT OF LIABILITY: $1,000,000 each occurrence\n\nThis certificate is issued for information only and confers no rights upon the holder beyond those of the policy.\n\nCertificate holder: City of Port Halden, Events Office\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Medical cover for the Dockside City Race 10K, Sunday 8 August 2027\n\nFrom Rhys Morgan, Race Director, Dockside Sports Trust\n\nThe race is a 10K with 800 runners and starts at 10:00. No ambulance will be stationed at the race; any ambulance would come through the 911 system.\n\nFirst aid\nWe'll have 3 first aid posts, at the start, the finish and halfway, with 8 trained first aiders between them, so nobody on the course is more than about a kilometre and a half from help. We also have two first aiders on bikes, carrying defibrillators.\n\nHeat, cold and water\nWe always tell runners to dress sensibly for the weather and to keep drinking, and it's all in the email we send them the week before. We'll be watching the forecast, and people here are used to all sorts of weather.\n\nIf someone needs hospital\nIf someone needed the hospital we'd dial 911 and the paramedics would take it from there. They know what they're doing far better than we do, and the city's service is very good.\n\nStaying in touch\nWe'll all have our phones, and I'll send a list of numbers round the team the week before. The signal is usually fine around there.\n\nWho's responsible\nOur medical lead is Yuki Tanaka, a registered paramedic, who'll be there from an hour before the start until the last runner is in and has the final word on pulling any runner out.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nDockside City Race 10K | Sunday 8 August 2027\nOrganiser: Dockside Sports Trust\nRace director: Rhys Morgan\nReference: EV-35850\n\nOverview\nThe Dockside City Race 10K is a 10K race of 10 km for 800 entrants, based in the Eastfield area of Port Halden. The start is at 10:00 and the course closes at 12:00.\n\nCourse\nThe course stays entirely on the Old Mill Trail and the Reservoir Walk, away from the highway, and no road is closed for the race. The finish is at the pavilion.\n\nCourse dimensions\nUsable width on the Old Mill Trail is 10 m and on the Reservoir Walk 10 m, with lawn or open paving beside the course for almost the whole distance. The finish area measures roughly 120 m by 60 m.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the old mill car park from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Dockside website the same day.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "24 April 2027\n\nEvents Office\nCity of Port Halden\n\nDear Events Officer,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nWe are applying for a street race permit for the Dockside City Race 10K on Sunday 8 August 2027. We expect 800 runners over 10K, starting at 10:00 in the Eastfield area. The completed form and the attachments (crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt) are enclosed.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRhys Morgan\nRace Director, Dockside Sports Trust\nrhys@docksidesports.example / 555-0152\n",
